/* SelectionSort_r: intermediate level of SelectionSort, written by hand (PipelineB, refinement step),
   the component BART refines.
   Purpose: restate the result of sort in the form the loop establishes, the permutation written
   cell by cell, rr(xx) = array(bij(xx)). The proof that this form implies the one of SelectionSort
   (composition (bij ; array), range ran(array)) is thus done once, here, away from the loop.
   array stays the concrete variable of SelectionSort; set_cell and the initialisation are unchanged.
   Same shape as ReverseArray_r and FillArray_r, the levels with an inherited concrete variable BART
   has refined: an INVARIANT clause restating the type of array, and an ANY, taken by a structure
   rule. The two quantifiers of sort over positions use the same name, xx: the rule has one joker
   for it. */
REFINEMENT
    SelectionSort_r

REFINES
    SelectionSort

SEES
    Ctx_SelectionSort

INVARIANT
    array : (0..max_IDX) --> INT

INITIALISATION
    array := (0..max_IDX) * {0}

OPERATIONS

    set_cell(pos, value) =
    PRE
        pos : IDX &
        value : INT
    THEN
        array(pos) := value
    END;

    sort =
    ANY rr WHERE
        rr : (0..max_IDX) --> INT &
        !xx.(xx : 0..max_IDX - 1 => rr(xx) <= rr(xx + 1)) &
        #bij.(bij : (0..max_IDX) >->> (0..max_IDX) &
              !xx.(xx : 0..max_IDX => rr(xx) = array(bij(xx))))
    THEN
        array := rr
    END

END
